<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000067> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001328> ;
                                                   rdfs:label "Civil Time Reference System"@en ;
                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Temporal Reference System that is a statutory time scale as designated by civilian authorities to determine local time(s)."@en ;
                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "In traditional astronomical usage, civil time is mean solar time as calculated from midnight as the beginning of the Civil Day."@en ,
                                                                                                   "Note that Civil Time Reference System is more accurately represented as a Temporal Reference System that participates in an act of usage that is sanctioned by an appropriate civil authority. As such, it should be represented as a defined class."@en ;
